<section aria-labelledby="faq-h" style="background:#E8F2EE;padding:clamp(48px,5.5vw,80px) 0">
<div style="max-width:1296px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(24px,4vw,48px);display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,340px),1fr));gap:clamp(32px,5vw,64px);align-items:start">
<div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px"><h2 id="faq-h" style="font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,36px);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em">AI Receptionist questions</h2><a href="/faq?topic=rec" style="font-weight:600;font-size:16px">See all questions →</a></div>
<div class="faq-span" style="border-bottom:1px solid #DED5C6">
<details open="" style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x4" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Will callers know they're talking to an AI?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Yes. The AI Receptionist introduces itself as an AI at the start of every call.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x5" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">What happens when the AI doesn't know an answer?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">It says so and routes the question to a person on your team, with the caller's callback details. It answers only from your approved knowledge.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x6" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Can it book appointments?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Yes. Booking appointments directly is part of the standard service.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x7" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Are calls recorded, and who can hear them?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Recordings and transcripts stay in your isolated environment. Only authorized users in your organization can access them.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x8" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">Will it call or text people on its own?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">No. It answers inbound calls only. All automated messages follow workflows you approve.</p></details>
<details style="border-top:1px solid #DED5C6"><summary class="x9" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px 0;font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(17px,1.5vw,19px);line-height:1.4">How is the AI Receptionist priced?<span class="hm-plus ms" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:26px;color:#0F4C45;transition:transform .15s">add</span></summary><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#2F3633;padding:0 0 24px;max-width:64ch">Pricing is custom, based on your use case and complexity. It's month-to-month with no setup fee for the standard service, and usage is billed at actual provider cost with no markup.</p></details>
</div>
